        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ios): implement branded typography design system",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe iOS app uses system fonts with inline `.font()` modifiers scattered across 50+ view files, making it impossible to enforce consistent typography or rebrand without touching every file.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nEstablishes a branded design system foundation:\n- **Typography tokens** (`OpenClawType`) backed by three bundled typefaces (Plus Jakarta Sans, DM Sans, JetBrains Mono) with full Dynamic Type scaling\n- **Spacing and radius tokens** (`OpenClawSpacing`, `OpenClawRadius`) replacing hardcoded numeric literals\n- **Additive brand color tokens** (accentPressed, teal, void, obsidian, slate, textPrimary, textSecondary)\n- **Shared components** (OpenClawToggleIndicator, OpenClawStatusBadge, button styles)\n- **Font license provenance** (SIL OFL 1.1 for all three families)\n\nAll iOS views are migrated to use `OpenClawType` tokens. No behavioral, navigation, or routing changes — this is purely visual/typographic.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Consistent branded typography across all screens\n- Proper Dynamic Type accessibility support via UIFontMetrics\n- Design tokens enable future theming without per-file changes\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Local `xcodebuild build` succeeds with zero errors\n- `pnpm native:i18n:check` passes\n- No behavioral changes to RootTabs, gateway problem banner, onboarding reset, Settings routing, or phone navigation\n\n## Font Provenance\n\n| Family | License | Source |\n|--------|---------|--------|\n| Plus Jakarta Sans | SIL OFL 1.1 | https://github.com/tokotype/PlusJakartaSans |\n| DM Sans | SIL OFL 1.1 | https://github.com/googlefonts/dm-fonts |\n| JetBrains Mono | SIL OFL 1.1 | https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono |\n\nFull license text included at `apps/ios/Sources/Fonts/LICENSE`.\n\n— [Joel Nishanth](https://offlyn.ai) · [offlyn.AI](https://offlyn.ai)",
        "branch": "feat/ios-design-system",
